Subject: [PATCH] isideload: give watchOS App IDs the App Group too

Upstream `Sideloader::sign_app` iterates over every App ID created for the IPA,
but skips the ones that belong to the watch app:

    for app_id in app_ids.iter_mut() {
        if watch_bundle_ids.contains(&app_id.identifier) {
            continue;                       // <-- watch App ID never touched
        }
        app_id.ensure_group_feature(...).await?;      // APG3427HIY
        self.dev_session.assign_app_group(..., None).await?;
        ...
    }

Consequences on a sideloaded watchOS companion:

  * the watch App ID never gets the App Groups capability (APG3427HIY)
  * no `group.*` identifier is assigned to it
  * the provisioning profile generated for the watch bundle therefore has no
    `com.apple.security.application-groups` entitlement
  * at runtime the watch app has an empty `GroupContainers` and dies with
    "An App Group ID may be missing" when it touches the shared container

Fix: treat watch App IDs like any other, but tag the Developer API calls with
`DeveloperDeviceType::Watchos` so that `DTDK_Platform=watchos` is added to the
request body. Without that marker Apple cannot resolve a watch App ID and the
update fails.

`DeveloperDeviceType` is already imported in this file, and both
`ensure_group_feature` (app_ids.rs) and `assign_app_group` (app_groups.rs)
already accept `impl Into<Option<DeveloperDeviceType>>` upstream, so this is a
single-hunk change with no other source edits.

diff --git a/iloader-main/vendor/isideload/isideload/src/sideload/sideloader.rs b/iloader-main/vendor/isideload/isideload/src/sideload/sideloader.rs
--- a/iloader-main/vendor/isideload/isideload/src/sideload/sideloader.rs
+++ b/iloader-main/vendor/isideload/isideload/src/sideload/sideloader.rs
@@ -151,16 +151,20 @@
             .await?;
 
         for app_id in app_ids.iter_mut() {
-            if watch_bundle_ids.contains(&app_id.identifier) {
-                continue;
-            }
+            // PATCH: watch App IDs must also receive the App Group, otherwise a
+            // sideloaded watchOS companion cannot reach its shared container.
+            let device_type = if watch_bundle_ids.contains(&app_id.identifier) {
+                Some(DeveloperDeviceType::Watchos)
+            } else {
+                None
+            };
 
             app_id
-                .ensure_group_feature(&mut self.dev_session, &team)
+                .ensure_group_feature(&mut self.dev_session, &team, device_type.clone())
                 .await?;
 
             self.dev_session
-                .assign_app_group(&team, &app_group, app_id, None)
+                .assign_app_group(&team, &app_group, app_id, device_type)
                 .await?;
 
             if increased_memory_limit {
